NAME
    build.sh - build one staged m-boot GRUB image and external loader tree

SYNOPSIS
    ./build.sh --target x86_64-efi|arm64-efi|i386-pc --output DIR
               [--modules-dir DIR] [--grub-mkimage PATH]

DESCRIPTION
    Standalone Linux build: needs grub-mkimage with target-specific modules
    and tar. Uses the source boot/ files to produce an embedded memdisk, then
    stages the external loader/ directory beneath data/m/boot/loader/.
    Does not install, partition, format, or write to a block device.
    Fails rather than replacing an existing DIR/TARGET.

TARGETS
    x86_64-efi: DIR/x86_64-efi/esp/EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI
    arm64-efi:  DIR/arm64-efi/esp/EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI
    i386-pc:   DIR/i386-pc/bios/core.img (not directly bootable by copying)
    Every target includes data/m/boot/loader/ and stage-info.

OPTIONS
    --target        Required GRUB image format.
    --output        Required parent of new staged build directories.
    --modules-dir   Optional target-specific GRUB module directory; required
                    when cross-target modules aren't in a standard location.
    --grub-mkimage  Optional explicit GRUB image generator executable/path.
    --help          Print usage.

EXAMPLES
    ./build.sh --target x86_64-efi --output ./dist
    ./build.sh --target arm64-efi --output ./dist \
      --modules-dir /usr/lib/grub/arm64-efi

PERSISTENT GRUB TARGET MODULE PACKAGES IN GIT
    The project stores the complete GRUB module directories and their
    corresponding m-boot boot stages as Git-tracked compressed archives:

        prebuilt/m-boot-x86_64-efi.tar.xz
        prebuilt/m-boot-arm64-efi.tar.xz
        prebuilt/m-boot-i386-pc.tar.xz

    Each archive has an adjacent .sha256 file. Contents of each archive:
        <target>/                 complete build stage (UEFI EFI executable or BIOS core)
        grub-modules/<target>/    complete target GRUB module directory
        <platform>-build-info.txt source commit and Ubuntu package versions
        BOOT*.EFI.sha256          checksum of built EFI executable (UEFI)
        core.img.sha256          checksum of built BIOS core (i386-pc)

    Use one common directory for all stages and modules:
        git pull --ff-only
        sha256sum -c prebuilt/m-boot-x86_64-efi.tar.xz.sha256
        sha256sum -c prebuilt/m-boot-arm64-efi.tar.xz.sha256
        sha256sum -c prebuilt/m-boot-i386-pc.tar.xz.sha256
        mkdir -p ./qemu-combined/stages
        tar -xJf prebuilt/m-boot-x86_64-efi.tar.xz \
          -C ./qemu-combined/stages
        tar -xJf prebuilt/m-boot-arm64-efi.tar.xz \
          -C ./qemu-combined/stages
        tar -xJf prebuilt/m-boot-i386-pc.tar.xz \
          -C ./qemu-combined/stages

    To rebuild any target with the unpacked module directory:
        ./build.sh --target x86_64-efi --output ./other-stages \
          --modules-dir ./qemu-combined/stages/grub-modules/x86_64-efi
        ./build.sh --target arm64-efi --output ./other-stages \
          --modules-dir ./qemu-combined/stages/grub-modules/arm64-efi
        ./build.sh --target i386-pc --output ./other-stages \
          --modules-dir ./qemu-combined/stages/grub-modules/i386-pc

    The corresponding GitHub Actions workflows build these packages on
    native ubuntu-24.04 (x86_64) and ubuntu-24.04-arm (ARM64) runners:
        .github/workflows/build-grub-x86_64.yml
        .github/workflows/build-grub-arm64.yml
        .github/workflows/build-grub-i386-pc.yml
    They also publish temporary Actions artifacts, but the tracked
    archives remain available with an ordinary git pull. The archives
    are versioned third-party GRUB binaries, not native source modules.
    Source/package provenance and usage details: prebuilt/README.md.
    The i386-pc archive contains boot.img for BIOS embedding; a host-side
    grub-bios-setup command is still required to install it into a disk image.
    GRUB modules and grub-mkimage should use compatible GRUB versions.


NOTES
    The tool checks for required GRUB modules but does not prove that firmware
    will boot the resulting image. Test with GRUB/QEMU before deployment.
    The legacy target-build.sh remains untouched.

